      "title": "PackShop — sell sealed Rapture card packs for native zkLTC and mint the cards to the buyer. PackShop is a separate contract from the card collection. It holds one role: MINTER on the Studio Test set's StudioMinter (the owner of that contract grants it with setMinter). It holds a pool of card TEMPLATES (a card's traits, stats and design record, copied from a finished card) and, on every pack, mints fresh tokens from those templates straight to the buyer. Templates are editions: a hundred wallets can hold a copy of the same design, each its own token with its own id. Flow (two transactions, so a buyer can never simulate and revert a bad pull):   1. buyPack()      pay the exact price; a sealed pack is recorded with the current block number   2. openPack(id)   once block.number >= commit + 2, the pack's cards are drawn from blockhash(commit + 1)                     and minted to the buyer. Anyone may send this transaction; the cards always go to the buyer. A pack nobody opens inside the blockhash window (255 block numbers, ~50 min on Liteforge) is refunded with refundExpired(id). TESTNET-GRADE RANDOMNESS. Liteforge is an Arbitrum Nitro chain: block.number follows the parent chain (one number every ~12 s), block.prevrandao is the constant 1, and Arbitrum documents blockhash as \"cryptographically insecure\". A commit-reveal on it stops the buyer from grinding, but the sequencer can still see or influence the seed. Before real value rides on a pull, replace _seed() with a VRF or drand beacon.",
      "version": 1
    },
    "userdoc": {
      "kind": "user",
      "methods": {
        "REVEAL_WINDOW()": {
          "notice": "The blockhash window, less one number so a pack is never opened on the edge of it."
        },
        "addTemplates((uint8,(uint8,uint8,uint8,uint8,uint32,uint16,uint16,uint16,uint16),(uint64,address,uint256),(bytes32,bytes32,bytes32,bytes32,bytes32,bytes32,bytes32,uint8,string,string))[])": {
          "notice": "Load cards the shop may mint. Each is checked against the same rules StudioMinter and CardDesign apply at mint time, so a paid pack cannot draw a template that would revert."
        },
        "config()": {
          "notice": "One call for a client: everything it needs to draw the buy button."
        },
        "constructor": {
          "notice": "Deploys PAUSED: load the templates, then unpause."
        },
        "dailyLimit()": {
          "notice": "Packs one wallet may buy per UTC day; 0 = no limit."
        },
        "liability()": {
          "notice": "Wei paid for packs that are still sealed. The owner can only withdraw the balance above it."
        },
        "openPack(uint256)": {
          "notice": "Draw and mint a sealed pack. Anyone may call; the buyer always receives the cards."
        },
        "packCountOf(address)": {
          "notice": "How many packs `who` has ever bought."
        },
        "packSize()": {
          "notice": "Cards per pack, fixed for this deployment (a different size is a new PackShop)."
        },
        "price()": {
          "notice": "Exact price of one pack, in wei of the native token (zkLTC)."
        },
        "ready()": {
          "notice": "Can the shop sell? Every Kind that has odds needs an active template (or a paid pack could not be drawn), and PackShop must hold the MINTER role on StudioMinter (or it could not be opened)."
        },
        "recentPacks(address,uint256)": {
          "notice": "`who`'s most recent `n` packs (at most 16), oldest first: id, phase and commit block of each. One call is all a page needs to resume a sealed pack (Waiting / Openable) or offer a refund (Expired)."
        },
        "refundExpired(uint256)": {
          "notice": "Give the price back for a pack that was not opened inside the blockhash window. Anyone may call; the refund goes to the buyer. The pack still counts against the buyer's daily limit."
        },
        "renounceOwnership()": {
          "notice": "Revenue is only reachable through the owner: renouncing would strand it."
        },
        "retireTemplate(uint256)": {
          "notice": "Stop minting a template. Cards already minted from it are untouched. The last template of a Kind that has odds cannot be retired (add its replacement first, or set that Kind's odds to 0)."
        },
        "weights(uint256)": {
          "notice": "Odds per slot of a pack, Mortal, King, Demigod, Titan, God. Only the ratio matters."
        },
        "withdraw(address,uint256)": {
          "notice": "Revenue only: the balance above what sealed packs could still be refunded."
        }
      },
      "version": 1
    }
